      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/scobiancistrus_aureatus_l_14_en/",
      "html": "<p>A male Scobiancistrus aureatus of about 30 cm in length may have reached full growth. The strong spines on the gill cover (interopercular odontodes) and on the pectoral fins are remarkable.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/scobiancistrus_aureatus_l_14_en/",
      "html": "<p>Brazil, Rio Xingu.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/scobiancistrus_aureatus_l_14_en/",
      "html": "<p>Like most L-catfishes from the Rio Xingu, they prefer warm water. The water temperature should not fall durably below 26°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/scobiancistrus_aureatus_l_14_en/",
      "html": "<p>Breeding has not yet succeeded as far as is known. It will surely require higher temperatures; most L-catfishes from the Xingu are bred at temperatures between 28°C and 30°C.</p>"
    }
  ],
